💡 **SUGGESTION: the `tracker` hand-off to token-usage comments is never asserted**

This line introduces the mechanism that keeps token-usage summary comments provider-correct (they go through the same tracker as the script's own comments instead of `postTokenUsageComments`' default jira fallback). None of the new/updated suites assert it — `test_triggerStoryTestAutomation.js` mocks `postTokenUsageComments: function(key, opts)` and ignores `opts`, and `test_wave1aTrackerMigration.js` stubs the helper as a noop.

Since the hand-off is the actual behavioral change on this line, consider capturing it once, e.g. in the wave1a `triggerStoryTestAutomation` ado test:

```js
'./common/tokenUsageComment.js': {
    postTokenUsageComments: function(key, opts) { tokenUsageOpts.push(opts); }
},
...
assert.equal(tokenUsageOpts[0].tracker.provider(), 'ado');
```

Without that assertion, a future refactor could silently drop `tracker: tracker` and all suites would stay green while token-usage comments regress to the jira default on ado/github deployments.

